1
00:00:08,628 --> 00:00:10,971
A dog barks suddenly behind you.

2
00:00:11,051 --> 00:00:15,631
Before you know what it is, your shoulders
have jumped. Your breath has stopped.

3
00:00:15,711 --> 00:00:17,674
Your heart is already racing.

4
00:00:18,472 --> 00:00:20,978
Something in you knew, before you did.

5
00:00:21,788 --> 00:00:24,783
For many years the rainbow
body has interested me.

6
00:00:24,863 --> 00:00:26,903
I wanted to read it in a balanced way.

7
00:00:26,983 --> 00:00:29,701
Not dismissing it, and not inflating it.

8
00:00:29,781 --> 00:00:34,049
And I found that this is not possible
until four things are sorted out.

9
00:00:34,129 --> 00:00:35,938
Each one has its own video.

10
00:00:36,018 --> 00:00:39,529
Leave any one of them out, and
the picture tips to one side.

11
00:00:40,344 --> 00:00:44,059
The first is the energy practices
of the different traditions.

12
00:00:44,139 --> 00:00:49,277
Taoist inner alchemy, Indian yoga and
the Tibetan yogas all work with breath,

13
00:00:49,357 --> 00:00:52,551
posture, an inner channel, heat and light.

14
00:00:52,631 --> 00:00:55,622
Their method is shared. Their view is not.

15
00:00:55,702 --> 00:01:00,051
Without sorting this out, the rainbow
body looks like an energy achievement,

16
00:01:00,131 --> 00:01:03,203
as if steering the winds
could turn a body into light.

17
00:01:03,283 --> 00:01:08,094
And wind, or energy, quietly becomes
a hidden stuff underneath everything.

18
00:01:08,174 --> 00:01:10,268
But the winds are not a substrate.

19
00:01:10,348 --> 00:01:13,217
Working with them can
loosen what the body holds.

20
00:01:13,297 --> 00:01:17,841
What frees is seeing through the habit
of reification, not where the winds go.

21
00:01:18,652 --> 00:01:20,913
The second is the five elements.

22
00:01:20,993 --> 00:01:24,174
Tibet keeps two different
fives side by side.

23
00:01:24,254 --> 00:01:29,174
One came from China: wood,
fire, earth, metal and water,

24
00:01:29,254 --> 00:01:31,484
used for the calendar and divination.

25
00:01:31,564 --> 00:01:35,601
The other came from
India: earth, water, fire,

26
00:01:35,681 --> 00:01:41,498
wind and space, read as qualities.
Hardness. Cohesion. Warmth.

27
00:01:41,578 --> 00:01:43,223
Motion. Room.

28
00:01:43,303 --> 00:01:46,294
The rainbow body belongs
to the Indian five.

29
00:01:46,374 --> 00:01:50,723
Without sorting this out, the five
lights get mixed with Chinese phases,

30
00:01:50,803 --> 00:01:52,802
or with modern physics of light.

31
00:01:52,882 --> 00:01:57,367
Or the elements are heard as energy
frozen into matter, waiting to melt back.

32
00:01:57,447 --> 00:02:02,014
Nothing freezes. The elements name
how appearing is felt and taken,

33
00:02:02,094 --> 00:02:03,567
not a stuff underneath.

34
00:02:04,376 --> 00:02:06,760
The third is the reports themselves.

35
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:10,985
What do the traditions actually
claim, and how strong is the evidence?

36
00:02:11,065 --> 00:02:17,065
Dzogchen, Gelug, Kālacakra, Bön and the
Taoist accounts each tell it differently,

37
00:02:17,193 --> 00:02:21,909
and with different views. The modern cases
rest on the word of those who were there.

38
00:02:21,989 --> 00:02:24,558
None has been checked
by anyone independent.

39
00:02:24,638 --> 00:02:29,069
Without sorting this out, the stories
are either swallowed whole as proof,

40
00:02:29,149 --> 00:02:33,281
or thrown out as myth. Both miss
what the traditions themselves say:

41
00:02:33,361 --> 00:02:36,479
the rainbow body is not
the measure of insight.

42
00:02:37,284 --> 00:02:39,450
The fourth is how the body knows.

43
00:02:39,530 --> 00:02:44,015
This is the one I have not yet set out,
and it is what this video is about.

44
00:02:44,095 --> 00:02:48,227
Without it, the rainbow body is
read in one of two wrong ways.

45
00:02:48,307 --> 00:02:53,486
Either everything is in the head, and the
body plays no part in realization at all.

46
00:02:53,566 --> 00:02:58,268
Or the body, its energy or its light,
becomes the ground of everything.

47
00:02:58,348 --> 00:03:02,208
The research, and my own
practice, point between the two.

48
00:03:02,288 --> 00:03:05,184
The body takes part in
knowing and in release.

49
00:03:05,264 --> 00:03:07,281
But it is not a deeper floor.

50
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:13,181
Put the four together, and a balanced
reading becomes possible. Not dismissing.

51
00:03:13,261 --> 00:03:16,754
Not inflating. The method
shared, the view not.

52
00:03:16,834 --> 00:03:19,907
The elements as qualities,
not a frozen stuff.

53
00:03:19,987 --> 00:03:21,782
The reports as reports.

54
00:03:21,862 --> 00:03:24,404
And the body as a place
where the knot is held,

55
00:03:24,484 --> 00:03:26,134
and where it comes undone.

56
00:03:26,948 --> 00:03:30,731
Its point is simple. Knowing
is not only analysis.

57
00:03:30,811 --> 00:03:33,693
It is not only the
taking apart of concepts.

58
00:03:33,773 --> 00:03:38,095
There is a more immediate knowing, the
felt sense of presence in the body.

59
00:03:38,175 --> 00:03:43,054
Through it, fear, clinging, openness and
spaciousness are often understood more

60
00:03:43,134 --> 00:03:45,025
directly than through thought alone.

61
00:03:45,105 --> 00:03:49,771
And the old traditions of inner winds were
long recognitions of this side of knowing.

62
00:03:50,568 --> 00:03:52,884
Let me start with the body that jumps.

63
00:03:53,692 --> 00:03:57,543
Modern research agrees with the
old traditions on one plain point.

64
00:03:57,623 --> 00:04:00,247
Much of our knowing
happens before we think.

65
00:04:00,327 --> 00:04:04,214
Deep in the brain are circuits that
detect threat and set off the heart,

66
00:04:04,294 --> 00:04:06,144
the hormones and the muscles.

67
00:04:06,224 --> 00:04:10,102
They work faster than conscious
thought, and largely beneath it.

68
00:04:10,904 --> 00:04:14,619
The body's learning can even be
split off from the mind's memory.

69
00:04:14,699 --> 00:04:18,790
In one study, a man with damage to
his memory centre could not remember a

70
00:04:18,870 --> 00:04:20,475
learning task at all.

71
00:04:20,555 --> 00:04:23,383
Yet his body still gave
the learned response.

72
00:04:23,463 --> 00:04:26,671
Another man, with damage to
the brain's alarm centre,

73
00:04:26,751 --> 00:04:28,383
remembered the task clearly.

74
00:04:28,463 --> 00:04:30,480
Yet his body had learned nothing.

75
00:04:31,284 --> 00:04:34,519
So a person can know perfectly
well that they are safe,

76
00:04:34,599 --> 00:04:39,184
and still find their body braced.
The breath held. The heart racing.

77
00:04:39,264 --> 00:04:42,880
Knowing that one is safe is not
only a conclusion of thought.

78
00:04:42,960 --> 00:04:46,444
Much of it is done by the body,
and thought arrives later.

79
00:04:47,248 --> 00:04:49,414
There is a quieter side of this too.

80
00:04:49,494 --> 00:04:53,015
The psychologist Eugene Gendlin
called it the felt sense.

81
00:04:53,095 --> 00:04:56,697
It is not a single sensation,
like an itch or warmth.

82
00:04:56,777 --> 00:05:00,039
It is a vague, whole-body
sense of a situation,

83
00:05:00,119 --> 00:05:03,558
all about this, that can be
noticed before it has words.

84
00:05:03,638 --> 00:05:08,395
When you attend to it and wait, a word
or an image often comes that fits.

85
00:05:08,475 --> 00:05:10,669
And the body eases as it does.

86
00:05:11,468 --> 00:05:14,354
Gendlin and his colleagues
found something striking.

87
00:05:14,434 --> 00:05:18,186
The people who gained most from therapy
were not those who talked best about their

88
00:05:18,266 --> 00:05:23,186
problems. They were the ones who could
sense this bodily feel, and stay with it.

89
00:05:23,266 --> 00:05:26,533
In some matters, this
knowing is the deciding one.

90
00:05:27,336 --> 00:05:31,703
Brain imaging shows the same
split, between knowing and telling.

91
00:05:31,783 --> 00:05:35,657
Researchers asked people to
attend to themselves in two ways.

92
00:05:35,737 --> 00:05:38,836
In one, they thought about
their traits and their story.

93
00:05:38,916 --> 00:05:43,483
In the other, they simply felt what
was present in the body, with no story.

94
00:05:43,563 --> 00:05:46,119
The two used different
networks in the brain.

95
00:05:46,199 --> 00:05:49,638
In people new to meditation,
the two were tightly bound.

96
00:05:49,718 --> 00:05:52,532
Every sensation set off
a judgment about me.

97
00:05:52,612 --> 00:05:55,970
After eight weeks of mindfulness
training, they came apart.

98
00:05:56,050 --> 00:06:00,254
A sensation could be known directly,
without the story attached.

99
00:06:01,060 --> 00:06:04,680
Reading that, I was reminded
of how anatta is put.

100
00:06:04,760 --> 00:06:06,922
In the seen, only the seen.

101
00:06:07,002 --> 00:06:09,195
In the felt, only the felt.

102
00:06:09,992 --> 00:06:12,280
But there is a catch, and it matters.

103
00:06:12,360 --> 00:06:17,579
Researchers now think the brain does not
simply read the body. It predicts it.

104
00:06:17,659 --> 00:06:22,389
What rises from the body is mostly the
gap between what was expected and what is

105
00:06:22,469 --> 00:06:26,030
found. This explains why
felt knowing is direct.

106
00:06:26,110 --> 00:06:28,082
It does not pass through reasoning.

107
00:06:28,162 --> 00:06:30,935
And it explains why felt
knowing can be wrong.

108
00:06:31,015 --> 00:06:36,207
If old expectations are set to danger, an
ordinary heartbeat is felt as a threat.

109
00:06:36,287 --> 00:06:39,495
The body then reports,
vividly and directly,

110
00:06:39,575 --> 00:06:41,307
a danger that is not there.

111
00:06:42,108 --> 00:06:44,342
Directness is no guarantee.

112
00:06:45,160 --> 00:06:49,813
Now fear. The treatments that work
best for fear do not argue it away.

113
00:06:49,893 --> 00:06:52,910
They let the body meet
what it fears, in safety,

114
00:06:52,990 --> 00:06:56,443
until it learns from experience
that the threat does not come.

115
00:06:56,523 --> 00:06:59,853
That is new learning in the
body, not a better argument.

116
00:06:59,933 --> 00:07:03,169
Some body-based therapies
do the same, more gently.

117
00:07:03,249 --> 00:07:08,390
In small, paced steps, so the body's
alarm can settle without being flooded.

118
00:07:09,188 --> 00:07:10,634
Clinging is the same.

119
00:07:10,714 --> 00:07:14,493
Attachment is not only a belief
that something will make me happy.

120
00:07:14,573 --> 00:07:16,667
It is a lean of the body toward it.

121
00:07:16,747 --> 00:07:18,623
A tightening when it is threatened.

122
00:07:18,703 --> 00:07:20,729
A held breath when it is lost.

123
00:07:20,809 --> 00:07:23,071
You can feel it before you can say it.

124
00:07:23,880 --> 00:07:25,788
I have written about this before.

125
00:07:25,868 --> 00:07:30,109
The habit of taking things as existing
from their own side does not live only in

126
00:07:30,189 --> 00:07:34,755
ideas. It lives in the muscles,
the diaphragm and the breath.

127
00:07:34,835 --> 00:07:37,228
A slight tightening behind the eyes.

128
00:07:37,308 --> 00:07:40,516
A held, high chest. A guarded belly.

129
00:07:40,596 --> 00:07:43,315
A subtle leaning forward
into the next moment,

130
00:07:43,395 --> 00:07:45,670
as if you had to hold the world together.

131
00:07:46,468 --> 00:07:49,531
When the view loosens, that
bracing loosens with it.

132
00:07:49,611 --> 00:07:52,941
In my own experience, when
the hinge in the view let go,

133
00:07:53,021 --> 00:07:55,468
the knot in the body uncoiled on its own.

134
00:07:55,548 --> 00:07:57,348
I was not forcing anything.

135
00:07:58,160 --> 00:08:02,242
Openness and spaciousness are known
the same way, from the other side.

136
00:08:02,322 --> 00:08:07,052
When the bracing goes, the release
is not first a thought. It is felt.

137
00:08:07,132 --> 00:08:12,926
The chest unclenches. The breath
drops. The edges soften. There is room.

138
00:08:13,740 --> 00:08:15,961
Here the science has little to say yet.

139
00:08:16,041 --> 00:08:20,363
These are qualities the contemplative
traditions have mapped far more fully than

140
00:08:20,443 --> 00:08:21,667
any laboratory.

141
00:08:21,747 --> 00:08:26,232
In one Tibetan teaching, fear and
grasping are not fought or argued with,

142
00:08:26,312 --> 00:08:28,596
since that only feeds the agitation.

143
00:08:28,676 --> 00:08:31,952
They are met in stillness,
silence and spaciousness,

144
00:08:32,032 --> 00:08:34,452
where the contraction
can loosen from within.

145
00:08:34,532 --> 00:08:36,463
That is a report of their tradition.

146
00:08:36,543 --> 00:08:38,411
It matches what I have found.

147
00:08:39,208 --> 00:08:41,564
So the old traditions saw this too.

148
00:08:42,380 --> 00:08:45,058
Tibetan medicine says
the mind rides the wind,

149
00:08:45,138 --> 00:08:46,761
like a rider on a horse.

150
00:08:46,841 --> 00:08:49,003
Causality runs both ways.

151
00:08:49,083 --> 00:08:50,973
Desire disturbs the wind.

152
00:08:51,053 --> 00:08:53,976
But once the wind is disturbed, by shock,

153
00:08:54,056 --> 00:08:59,601
worry, overwork or poor food, it
disturbs the mind. Racing thoughts.

154
00:08:59,681 --> 00:09:03,120
Panic. Poor sleep. Frightening dreams.

155
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:06,000
And since no argument
calms a bolting horse,

156
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:11,584
the treatment is bodily. Warm
food. Oil massage. Warm compresses.

157
00:09:11,664 --> 00:09:13,029
A calmer life.

158
00:09:13,824 --> 00:09:17,308
The Tibetan yogas of breath
and movement work the same way.

159
00:09:17,388 --> 00:09:20,406
They settle the winds,
and so settle the mind.

160
00:09:20,486 --> 00:09:25,216
In one trial at a large cancer centre,
women having chemotherapy who practised

161
00:09:25,296 --> 00:09:28,626
such a programme slept with fewer
disturbances than those who only

162
00:09:28,706 --> 00:09:32,516
stretched. They were not,
though, less tired overall.

163
00:09:33,316 --> 00:09:37,751
The Taoists, too, worked the body,
the breath and attention together.

164
00:09:37,831 --> 00:09:41,909
Their inner alchemy held that mind-nature
and bodily life must be cultivated

165
00:09:41,989 --> 00:09:46,039
together. Insight without the
body's vitality, they said,

166
00:09:46,119 --> 00:09:48,353
stays stuck in empty stillness.

167
00:09:49,160 --> 00:09:53,487
And the Buddha refused to trace
every bodily feeling to past action.

168
00:09:53,567 --> 00:09:56,693
He named bile, phlegm
and wind, the weather,

169
00:09:56,773 --> 00:09:59,573
careless habits and injury as causes too.

170
00:09:59,653 --> 00:10:04,374
And he taught mindfulness of the
breath, the posture and the body itself.

171
00:10:05,172 --> 00:10:06,849
These are not anatomies.

172
00:10:06,929 --> 00:10:10,980
The words for wind, in
Tibet, in India and in China,

173
00:10:11,060 --> 00:10:14,662
first meant wind and breath,
not a stuff called energy.

174
00:10:14,742 --> 00:10:17,827
The channels and the winds
are maps of how breath,

175
00:10:17,907 --> 00:10:21,672
feeling and attention move
together, drawn from the inside.

176
00:10:21,752 --> 00:10:25,300
Read that way, the traditions
are accurate about what they map.

177
00:10:25,380 --> 00:10:30,305
The felt movement of experience, and
how mind and body condition each other.

178
00:10:31,120 --> 00:10:35,107
To stay balanced, I should say
what the research does not show.

179
00:10:35,924 --> 00:10:39,621
It does not show that trauma is
stored in muscle or connective tissue,

180
00:10:39,701 --> 00:10:41,256
waiting to be shaken out.

181
00:10:41,336 --> 00:10:44,123
That is a popular story, not a finding.

182
00:10:44,203 --> 00:10:48,987
The theory many therapists use to explain
the nervous system is strongly disputed by

183
00:10:49,067 --> 00:10:50,848
the scientists who study it.

184
00:10:50,928 --> 00:10:53,810
And the body-based trauma
therapies are promising,

185
00:10:53,890 --> 00:10:56,885
but not yet proven against
the established ones.

186
00:10:57,696 --> 00:11:00,107
What is well supported is the main point.

187
00:11:00,187 --> 00:11:02,131
The body knows before thought.

188
00:11:02,211 --> 00:11:04,210
The felt sense guides change.

189
00:11:04,290 --> 00:11:07,131
Fear is unlearned through
bodily experience.

190
00:11:07,211 --> 00:11:10,705
And knowing one's story, and
directly feeling the body,

191
00:11:10,785 --> 00:11:12,462
run on different paths.

192
00:11:13,276 --> 00:11:14,804
So where do I stand?

193
00:11:15,848 --> 00:11:19,454
Felt knowing is a kind of
insight, not only energy work.

194
00:11:19,534 --> 00:11:22,131
When fear or clinging
is seen as it is felt,

195
00:11:22,211 --> 00:11:25,908
as this contraction, this
held breath, this lean toward,

196
00:11:25,988 --> 00:11:27,906
that seeing is itself insight.

197
00:11:27,986 --> 00:11:30,025
It does not wait for a concept.

198
00:11:30,105 --> 00:11:32,842
And it often frees more
than the concept would.

199
00:11:33,636 --> 00:11:37,079
Contemplative scientists draw
the line in the same place.

200
00:11:37,159 --> 00:11:39,919
They sort meditation into three families.

201
00:11:39,999 --> 00:11:44,036
The family of insight practice
aims at what they call reification,

202
00:11:44,116 --> 00:11:47,623
taking things as solid,
existing from their own side.

203
00:11:47,703 --> 00:11:52,079
And its method is direct inquiry
into experience, not argument.

204
00:11:52,159 --> 00:11:54,770
Deconstruction, in their sense as in mine,

205
00:11:54,850 --> 00:11:57,233
is a seeing, not only a reasoning.

206
00:11:58,048 --> 00:12:01,790
But two guards. This felt
knowing is more immediate.

207
00:12:01,870 --> 00:12:03,611
It is not more fundamental.

208
00:12:03,691 --> 00:12:06,750
It is older in evolution
and faster in time.

209
00:12:06,830 --> 00:12:09,983
But it is not a deeper
floor beneath experience.

210
00:12:10,063 --> 00:12:12,538
It arises in dependence, like any knowing,

211
00:12:12,618 --> 00:12:14,644
and it is as empty as what it knows.

212
00:12:14,724 --> 00:12:18,982
To make it a ground would bring the
substrate back, through the bodily door.

213
00:12:19,796 --> 00:12:21,772
And direct does not mean right.

214
00:12:21,852 --> 00:12:25,576
The body's sense of danger can
be a habit, not a perception.

215
00:12:25,656 --> 00:12:28,036
So felt knowing needs refining too.

216
00:12:28,116 --> 00:12:31,976
By experience, by gentle
attention, and by the view.

217
00:12:32,056 --> 00:12:35,739
The view tells the body what it
need no longer brace against.

218
00:12:35,819 --> 00:12:38,937
The body tells the view
whether it has truly landed.

219
00:12:39,744 --> 00:12:42,640
Analysis without the
body stays in the head,

220
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:45,552
and the body keeps its
old bracing underneath.

221
00:12:45,632 --> 00:12:48,554
Felt knowing without the
view can settle the body,

222
00:12:48,634 --> 00:12:51,734
yet leave untouched the
framework that made it brace.

223
00:12:51,814 --> 00:12:55,583
The street between insight
and the body runs both ways.

224
00:12:56,380 --> 00:12:58,900
And this is where it
meets the rainbow body.

225
00:12:59,720 --> 00:13:02,606
The body is not outside realization.

226
00:13:02,686 --> 00:13:05,364
The knot of reification
is held in the body,

227
00:13:05,444 --> 00:13:07,566
felt there, and released there.

228
00:13:07,646 --> 00:13:11,764
So it is fully reasonable that the
traditions speak of realization reaching

229
00:13:11,844 --> 00:13:16,782
all the way into the body, and of the
body itself being known without grasping.

230
00:13:17,580 --> 00:13:22,124
What is genuinely shown is that the body
takes part in knowing and in release.

231
00:13:22,204 --> 00:13:25,181
What is not shown is that
a corpse turns into light.

232
00:13:25,261 --> 00:13:27,355
I hold the first with confidence.

233
00:13:27,435 --> 00:13:30,090
The second, I hold as a report.

234
00:13:30,904 --> 00:13:34,578
Two cautions before I close.
This is not treatment.

235
00:13:34,658 --> 00:13:37,703
If you live with trauma,
panic or depression,

236
00:13:37,783 --> 00:13:42,078
practices like these are a help,
not a cure. And do not force.

237
00:13:42,158 --> 00:13:44,239
Settle, and do not strain.

238
00:13:44,319 --> 00:13:47,337
Pleasant openness in the
body is not awakening.

239
00:13:47,417 --> 00:13:50,357
Insight is measured by
the freedom of the mind.

240
00:13:51,164 --> 00:13:56,242
So, the dog barks again. The
shoulders jump. The breath stops.

241
00:13:57,048 --> 00:14:00,016
This time, notice it. Where it is held.

242
00:14:00,096 --> 00:14:02,638
How it feels, before it has a name.

243
00:14:02,718 --> 00:14:05,346
And whether anyone is found, holding it.

244
00:14:06,148 --> 00:14:07,771
The body knew first.

245
00:14:07,851 --> 00:14:10,425
Let it also be where
the knot comes undone.

